name: sim.getSimulatorMessage
description: Retrieves and removes the next message in the C/C++ or Lua message queues. Use this in a while-loop until all messages have been extracted. While the C/C++ interface has one single message queue, each Lua script has its own message queue. The C/C++ version of this function should only be called from the CoppeliaSim client application. A given message queue cannot hold more than 64 messages, unread messages will be discarded.
luaSynopsis: int message, list auxiliaryData, list auxiliaryData2 = sim.getSimulatorMessage()
pythonSynopsis: int message, int[4] auxiliaryData, int[] auxiliaryData2 = sim.getSimulatorMessage()
inputs:
outputs:
1. message: simulator message
2. auxiliaryData: array of numbers that describe the returned message in more details
3. auxiliaryData2: array of numbers that describe the returned message in more details
